{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"uncheering-ammonic-dalmatian","creation_channel":"cli","description":"Follow-up advisories from Gerrit change 2672 (c6ce) patchset-2 LLM-Review (PASS, non-blocking). Captured here so they are not lost after the corroborator lands.\n\n1. (correctness) Bound PEAK MEMORY of the terraform-config-inspect subprocess. src/rebar/grounding/terraform_corroborator.py:_run — proc.communicate(timeout=...) buffers the childs ENTIRE stdout/stderr into memory before the len(stdout) > MAX_STDOUT / MAX_STDERR check runs, so a runaway or hostile binary can OOM the host before the post-hoc cap is enforced. The 60s deadline bounds time but not memory. Fix: read both pipes incrementally under the deadline and abort (abstain worker_failure) once a running total exceeds the cap, instead of a post-communicate() length check. Threat is primarily a buggy/runaway legitimate binary on a large module (a malicious same-named binary on PATH already implies code-exec as the user).\n\n2. (maintainability) Dead filter clause in _minimal_env: `if k in _KEEP_ENV and not _drop_env(k)`. _KEEP_ENV is a closed allowlist (LANG, LC_ALL, LC_CTYPE, SYSTEMROOT, WINDIR, COMSPEC, PATHEXT) and none of its members match any _DROP_ENV_PREFIX, so `and not _drop_env(k)` is always True. Remove the dead conjunct (or add a comment justifying defence-in-depth) so the filter is not misleading.\n\n3. (tests) Strengthen non-disclosure on the MATCH path. tests/unit/grounding/test_terraform_corroborator.py::test_exact_declaration_matches_every_supported_class drives the corroborator with _module_json() whose variable description and default are both SECRET, but never asserts SECRET is absent from evidence+receipt on the positive match path (other abstain-path tests do). Add the assertion so the digest-only redaction is pinned on the match path too.\n\nAcceptance criteria: all three addressed with tests; corroborator suite + terraform seam suites green; no new LLM-Review blocking findings.","id":"ca1f-88ee-6211-4bff","parent_id":"a374-849c-c8f2-4234","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Corroborator PS2 advisories: bound subprocess memory, dead env filter, match-path non-disclosure test"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788602441866463001,"uuid":"25f84f29-48ad-4448-8882-6e07935357ac"}